# MatFinance — Setup Guide

A personal finance tracking system based on Google Sheets + Google Apps Script, featuring a local-first offline interface and background sync queue.

## 1. Google Sheet & Script Setup

1. Open your existing `MatFinance` Google Sheet.
2. From the menu, go to **Extensions → Apps Script**.
3. Replace the code in your `Code.gs` file with the updated `Code.gs` provided here.
4. Replace the code in your `Index.html` file with the updated `Index.html` provided here.
5. Save the project.

## 2. Important: Run Setup Again

Because we changed the categories to English and fixed the sync bug, you should re-initialize the sheet.
1. In the Apps Script editor, select `setupSpreadsheet` from the top function dropdown.
2. Click **Run**.
3. *Note: If you have existing transactions you want to keep, copy them somewhere safe first, as this will clear the sheets and apply the new English headers.*

## 3. Deploy the Updates

1. In the script editor, click **Deploy → Manage deployments**.
2. Click the **Edit (pencil icon)** on your active deployment.
3. Under **Version**, choose **New version**.
4. Click **Deploy**. *(If you don't do this, the live app will still run the old code!)*

## 4. Wrapper & App Installation

1. Update your `app.html` file on your hosting provider (Cloudflare/GitHub Pages) with the new one provided. Ensure you insert your `/exec` URL into the `GAS_APP_URL` variable.
2. Open the wrapper URL on your phone's browser (Safari or Chrome).
3. **Add to Home Screen:** Tap the share/menu button and select "Add to Home Screen". The new app icon will now appear correctly.
